@@ -3,3 +3,20 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from "./src/index.js";
+
+resolvePointer({ foo: ["bar", "baz"] }, "/foo/1"); // "baz"
+resolvePointer({ "a/b": 1 }, "/a~1b"); // 1
+resolvePointer(doc, ""); // the whole document
+```
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` returns the value the pointer refers to. It throws an `Error` when
+the pointer is not valid RFC 6901 syntax (for example it does not start with `/`, or contains `~` not
+followed by `0` or `1`), or when it does not resolve: a missing member, an array index that is out of
+range, has leading zeros or is `-` (the nonexistent element), or a step through a primitive or `null`.
+Only own properties are followed, so keys such as `__proto__` or `constructor` never reach the
+prototype chain. The document is not mutated.
