+
+# Request
+
+Implement JSON Pointer per RFC 6901 and export `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` from `src/index.ts`.
+It returns the value the pointer refers to, and throws when the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer
+(RFC 6901 section 3 syntax) or does not resolve to a value of the document (section 4).
+
+# Acceptance
+
+- `""` refers to the whole document; `/` refers to the key `""`.
+- `~1` decodes to `/` and `~0` to `~`, in that order (section 4); a `~` not followed by 0 or 1 is invalid.
+- A pointer not empty and not starting with `/` is invalid.
+- Array tokens must be `0` or digits without leading zeros; `-` (nonexistent element) and out-of-range indices throw.
+- Only own properties resolve (no prototype lookups such as `__proto__`); primitives and `null` cannot be traversed.
+- The document is never mutated. No runtime dependency.
+- Tests cover the RFC 6901 section 5 examples and the error cases.
